            ],
            "body": "- [x] How will a change to planned scope make the old readiness review visibly stale?\n  - Why it matters: an old approval of scope must not silently apply to new commitments.\n  - Next action: implement the fingerprint check and cover it with fixtures.\n  - Resolution: the review records a SHA-256 fingerprint of the scoped outcome, acceptance and relationships plus the review item text and targets; the checker reports unassessed when that input changes."
          },
          {
            "id": "Q2",
            "kind": "investigation",
            "state": "resolved",
            "appliesTo": [
              "m2"
            ],
            "blocks": [
              "m2"
            ],
            "body": "- [x] How do checked boxes distinguish a real answer from a deferral or a reopened question?\n  - Why it matters: a checkbox alone can make an unanswered decision appear closed.\n  - Next action: use explicit item state and require evidence for resolved/deferred states.\n  - Resolution: item metadata declares open, deferred or resolved; the checkbox must agree; resolved items require a Resolution line, deferred items require a reason, and reopened items preserve prior answers separately."
          },
